  "body": "`cut.yml` runs both its jobs on `runs-on: [self-hosted, linux]`. GitHub matches labels case-insensitively, and every post-merge runner is registered with `self-hosted,Linux,X64,camcraft-post-merge`. Since 2026-11-21 there are eight of them. So the release gate (up to 5 h, sized for 16 cores and 64 GB) can land on any of them, including 8-thread laptops and 24 GB boxes. The PR-test runner `len` once took a cut job the same way (2026-11-14).\n\nFor the cut of 2026-11-21, a stop-gap on the runner owner's side stops every runner except `wopr` while a release PR is open.\n\n## Change\n- `.github/workflows/cut.yml`: both `runs-on: [self-hosted, linux]` become `runs-on: [self-hosted, camcraft-cut]`.\n- AGENTS.md and `.claude/skills/runners/SKILL.md`: the cut runner carries the label `camcraft-cut`.\n\n## Merge order (important)\nMerge only **after** a runner has the `camcraft-cut` label: Settings -> Actions -> Runners -> `wopr` -> add label `camcraft-cut` (optionally `uma` as a backup). No re-registration is needed. If `cut.yml` asks for the label before any runner has it, the gate waits in the queue forever. Never merge it during a cut.\n\nDone means: `cut.yml` targets `camcraft-cut`, the docs name it, at least one runner carries the label, and the next cut's gate runs there.\n",
